(Code 1985, § 6-201)

232:
The intent of this article is to:
(1) Recognize trees to be a valuable asset providing a healthier and more beautiful environment in which to live;
(2) Recognize that trees are economically beneficial in attracting new residents, providing shade and cooling effects as well as preventing noise and pollution;
(3) Recognize that trees also prevent erosion and assist in flood control;
(4) Establish standards limiting the removal of, and ensuring the replacement of trees sufficient to safeguard the ecological and aesthetic environment necessary to a healthy, happy community;
(5) Not be punitive or to cause hardship to any individual, private or public company that uses care and diligence to protect trees within the city;
(6) Not affect private property of any sort except in the situation of public safety;
(7) Not affect new development projects in the private sector.
(Code 1985, § 6-601)
